WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:05.639
Your editor. Your terminal. Your browser. Your AI chat.

00:06.239 --> 00:10.002
Four windows, and none of them talk to each other.

00:12.500 --> 00:13.556
Meet Marven.

00:13.956 --> 00:18.717
An AI coding agent and a full code editor, in one desktop app.

00:21.000 --> 00:26.670
Ask for a change, and the agent reads your code, makes the edit, and runs your tests.

00:33.100 --> 00:39.720
Every edit shows up as a diff before it's written. Approve it, reject it, or roll it back.

00:41.500 --> 00:48.870
It's a real editor, too. Fourteen languages, a live terminal, and ⌘K to rewrite any selection.

00:51.100 --> 00:56.866
Bring your own model: Groq, OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter or NVIDIA.

00:57.266 --> 01:01.968
Or run it all locally, with Ollama, LM Studio or llama-server.

01:04.300 --> 01:08.863
Your files, your history and your memory stay on your machine.

01:09.263 --> 01:12.243
Pick a local model, and nothing leaves at all.

01:15.100 --> 01:21.220
It can even use a browser, and it asks before every new site and every form it submits.

01:23.500 --> 01:31.442
Talk to it with “Hey Marven”, plug in MCP servers, commit with git, and teach it your project’s rules.

01:34.200 --> 01:34.878
Marven.

01:35.478 --> 01:39.769
Free and open source, for Mac, Windows and Linux.
